# The build context is the repository root, which holds node_modules, .git, Terraform state and
# more. So this file is an allow-list: everything is left out except what the Dockerfile copies.
# (BuildKit reads "<Dockerfile name>.dockerignore" next to the Dockerfile before the one in the
# root of the context. The legacy builder does not; Docker Desktop and Compose v2 use BuildKit.)
*

!contracts/xsd/
!partner-sim/app/
!partner-sim/tests/
!partner-sim/requirements.txt
!partner-sim/requirements-dev.txt
!partner-sim/pyproject.toml

# Then again, inside the folders allowed above:
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
